# GMEOW native physical engine performance ledger.
# A first-class reasoning artifact flagging the deferred / non-incremental parts
# of the seven-lever execution stack. The built P0 levers (the relational core —
# semi-naive + stratified negation + index selection, selective worst-case-optimal
# joins, magic-sets, positive-Datalog signed incrementality, cached compiled plans,
# and bounded min-height / Z-weight provenance) are NOT
# rows here; this ledger records ONLY the deferred items, so a row is never
# misread as a shipped feature. Two honest statuses:
#   gmeow:FlaggedNonIncremental — a canonical hard part: a native fallback EXISTS,
#     it is simply not yet incremental and stays a heavy-path fallback longest.
#   gmeow:DeclaredP1 — an advanced lever intentionally out of the current scope:
#     NOT a defect, NOT yet built, a declared later stage.
# DO NOT EDIT.
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .

# --- ledger header (deferred / non-incremental rows only) ---
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/perf-ledger> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/PerfLedger> ;
   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/entryCount> 5 ;
   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "the deferred / non-incremental parts of the native physical engine's seven-lever stack; the built P0 levers are not rows here"@en .

# --- deferred / non-incremental entries ---
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/perf-entry-0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/PerfLedgerEntry> ;
   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/construct> "incremental well-founded / stable-model semantics"@en ;
   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/perfStatus> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/FlaggedNonIncremental> ;
   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/note> "well-founded / stable-model semantics incrementally stays a heavy-path fallback longest; a native fallback exists but is not yet incremental"@en .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/perf-entry-1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/PerfLedgerEntry> ;
   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/construct> "existential-rule chase with termination and incrementality together"@en ;
   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/perfStatus> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/FlaggedNonIncremental> ;
   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/note> "existential-rule chase with termination AND incrementality together stays a heavy-path fallback longest; a native fallback exists but is not yet incremental"@en .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/perf-entry-2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/PerfLedgerEntry> ;
   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/construct> "paraconsistent / modal facets"@en ;
   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/perfStatus> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/FlaggedNonIncremental> ;
   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/note> "the paraconsistent / modal facets stay heavy-path fallbacks longest; a native fallback exists but is not yet incremental"@en .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/perf-entry-3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/PerfLedgerEntry> ;
   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/construct> "rule-program-changing conjecture candidates"@en ;
   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/perfStatus> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/FlaggedNonIncremental> ;
   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/note> "ground fact candidates use the signed fixed-contract session; a candidate that changes the rule program has a native fallback but is not yet incremental"@en .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/perf-entry-4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/PerfLedgerEntry> ;
   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/construct> "bounded retractions and non-positive counterfactual programs"@en ;
   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/perfStatus> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/FlaggedNonIncremental> ;
   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/note> "unbounded positive counterfactual revisions use signed incremental maintenance; bounded retractions and programs with negation, builtins, or rule facts retain a native fallback but are not yet incremental"@en .
